course: dictionary
lesson: 3413
title: Exporters and trade
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An exporter is a person, company or country that sells goods to other countries. It comes from export, which means sending goods out of a country. The ending -er means someone who does the job, so an exporter is someone who exports.
explain: «Bangladesh is one of the biggest clothes exporters in the world.» The clue is that the clothes are made there and then sold abroad. So the word means a country that sells many clothes to other countries.
explain: «Ukraine is one of the world's biggest exporters of wheat, corn and sunflower oil.» When its Black Sea ports were blocked in 2022, food prices rose in many countries. This tells you that exporters depend on other countries to buy their goods.
fact: An exporter sends goods abroad, out of its own country.
fact: Australia is a major exporter of iron ore, New Zealand of milk products, and Canada of wood.
fact: The plural is exporters: one exporter, many exporters.
fact: The opposite of an exporter is an importer, who brings goods into a country from abroad.
fact: Useful phrases are «a major exporter of» and «the world's biggest exporter».
exercise: «Ukraine is one of the world's biggest exporters of wheat, corn and sunflower oil.» What is an exporter? | A person, company or country that buys goods from other countries | *A person, company or country that sells goods to other countries | A machine that makes food | A place where goods are stored before a journey
exercise: Which product is New Zealand a major exporter of? | Clothes | Iron ore | *Milk products | Sunflower oil
exercise: When Ukraine's Black Sea ports were blocked in 2022, why did food prices rise in many countries? | *Ukraine could not send its food exports out | Canada sent too much wood abroad | Everyone went on holiday at once | Children in Africa stopped eating food
test: Which phrase means a country that sells the most goods abroad? | A place to store goods | A quiet, gloomy sort of sad | *The world's biggest exporter | The main road into a city
test: What is the opposite of an exporter? | A tourist | *An importer | A teacher | A farmer
exam: In «Bangladesh is one of the biggest clothes exporters in the world», what does exporters mean? | Shops that sell clothes in the street | *Countries that sell clothes to other countries | Workers who sew clothes at home | Countries that make clothes for their own people
